# 📊 16. Important Fields to Investigate

When analyzing a `sudo` event, look for:

| Field                | What it tells you               |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Timestamp            | When the event occurred         |
| Username             | Who executed the command        |
| TTY                  | Terminal/session used           |
| PWD                  | Working directory               |
| USER                 | Account the command ran as      |
| COMMAND              | Command executed                |
| Source/login context | How the user reached the system |

These fields help establish the context of the activity.

