# 🚨 17. Suspicious sudo Indicators

Some activity may deserve additional investigation:

```text
Repeated sudo authentication failures
        ↓
Unexpected user using sudo
        ↓
Unusual administrative command
        ↓
Sudo activity immediately after unknown SSH login
        ↓
Unexpected command executed as root
```

Examples of commands that may deserve context-based investigation:

```text
useradd
usermod
passwd
chmod
chown
systemctl
iptables
```

These commands can be legitimate administrative tools, so their presence alone does not indicate malicious activity.

